Z||000007||Seanh||12-25-2000||05:47 PM||||A local shop told me $1800, plus the cost of the engine. Depending on where you live, it might be worth while to have a Fiero place like ED Parks or Fiero Shop or at least a "Fiero Friendly" Shop. Some one should have a site to locate the nearest "Fiero Friendly" shop. Just an Idea. I could host the site and maintain the page if some one could provide me with the information. Maybe Ill give it a shot.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/transsig.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.kdsi.net/~sean" TARGET=_blank>Sean's Fiero Page</A><BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8 Auto<BR>Going on to 3.4 in Jan.<BR><I>"It's always in the last place you look." Of course it is. Why would you keep looking after you've found it? Do people do this? Who and where are they?</I>||||reg||4
